{
  "id": "payback_time",
  "title": "Payback Time",
  "description": "Investments and payback time. Payback time is the number of periods required for cumulative benefits to equal cumulative costs. The smaller the payback period, the better the investment.",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Payback Time Calculator\n\nPayback time is the number of periods required for cumulative benefits to equal cumulative costs.\n\n### Undiscounted Payback\nF₀ = F₁ + F₂ + ... + Fₙₚ\n\nwhere:\n- F₀ = initial investment\n- F₁, F₂, etc. = cash flows in future periods\n- nₚ = period where initial investment equals accumulated future cash flows\n\n### Discounted Payback\nF₀ = F₁ / (1 + i) + F₂ / (1 + i)² + ... + Fₙₚ / (1 + i)ⁿₚ\n\nwhere:\n- i = interest rate (discount rate)"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "initial_investment",
          "label": "Initial Investment (F₀)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 10000,
          "unit": "$"
        },
        {
          "id": "interest_rate",
          "label": "Interest Rate (i)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 0.1,
          "unit": "%"
        },
        {
          "id": "discount_method",
          "label": "Payback Method",
          "type": "select",
          "options": [
            {
              "label": "Undiscounted",
              "value": "undiscounted"
            },
            {
              "label": "Discounted",
              "value": "discounted"
            }
          ],
          "defaultValue": "undiscounted"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "payback_period",
          "label": "Payback Period",
          "formula": "inputs.initial_investment",
          "unit": "periods"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Period",
        "Cash Flow",
        "Undiscounted Cumulative",
        "Discounted Cumulative"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
